# The three tiers, on one file. `check_it` is reached only by `validate
# :check_it`, `used_once` has exactly one written caller, and `never_used` has
# nothing — and `run` is not reported, because it is called from the class body
# of no one but is itself the caller.
#
# The distinction that took a bug to find: a symbol reference is tiered
# `possible`, so it sits *inside* the possible count. Subtracting it is what
# makes `convention-only` reachable at all — without that, a method reached
# only by a macro reads as an ordinary single caller.
symbols app.rb Widget,check_it,used_once,never_used,run
refs Widget#check_it confirmed=0 possible=1 excluded=0
refs Widget#never_used confirmed=0 possible=0 excluded=0
